+    # Growser-174 (was growser lesson 26, re-cut for Chromium 153): a .tlb is a
+    # binary type library, and a midl.exe from a different Windows SDK emits a
+    # handful of differing bytes - version and ordering noise - while the
+    # generated .h/.c stay byte-identical (measured: 10 bytes out of 2732). The
+    # build consumes the CHECKED-IN outputs; midl.exe runs only to verify them,
